# UPDATED 2026-08-10 for the local-naming SPLIT.
#
# Line 6 is `FCount` -- an F-prefixed local. It used to be asserted here as
# local-var-casing, because ONE rule fired for two unrelated complaints
# ("should be PascalCase AND not carry a field/param prefix"). It is now
# local-field-prefix: FCount is perfectly PascalCase, so calling it a CASING
# violation was always the wrong label, and the conflation buried the 22 real
# F-prefixed locals under 116 complaints about the loop counter `i`.
#
# The negative assertion below is the load-bearing one: it pins that an
# F-prefixed local is reported ONCE, under the prefix rule, and no longer also
# as a casing violation. Without it the split could regress into double-reporting.
local-field-prefix 6
!local-var-casing 6

# Line 7 is `ok` -- genuinely mis-cased, 2 characters, so NOT covered by the
# new 1-character exemption. Still local-var-casing, unchanged.
local-var-casing 7

# Line 9 is `GLE` -- a short all-caps initialism, exempt from casing as before.
!local-var-casing 9
